          "body": "Independent follow-up to #358. Compare SQLite and MariaDB through public snekql transactions and SQLAlchemy ORM sessions.\n\nInvestigate invalid assignment and update rejection stages, omitted versus explicit NULL patch fields, transaction/session reuse after a failed write, object state after commit/rollback versus independent reads, and decoding of externally corrupted rows.\n\nKeep idiomatic behavior separate from added validation policies. The specification is the oracle, not either library. Use isolated databases and test-first research checks; retain runnable probes and observed evidence. No package fixes, literal-default design decisions, or merging previous PRs.\n",
